  "id": "e230cda3-1998-460a-b62e-17f17afbd6cb",
  "title": "X-chromosome inactivation drives L1 retrotransposon enrichment on the human X chromosome",
  "summary": "X-chromosome inactivation (XCI) enables gene dosage compensation in XX eutherians, while L1 retrotransposons are hypothesized to facilitate this process. Long interspersed element-1 (LINE-1 or L1) retrotransposons are found to be especially abundant on the human X chromosome, and their preferential insertion into the inactive X chromosome likely contributes to their enrichment.",
  "facts": [
